From c8f8df2410300a83ce113bc450414235dd075c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yocto Port <elmermetrasbrum@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:56:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: radxa-zero-3e: enable NPU

The rknpu and rknpu_mmu nodes default to status = "disabled" in the
shared rk356x.dtsi (both nodes, checked directly:
arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi). The backported board dtsi
(0004-*.patch) only set rknpu-supply, without enabling either node -
NPU stayed off. rknpu_mmu (its IOMMU, referenced via
'iommus = <&rknpu_mmu>;' in the rknpu node) needs enabling too, or the
NPU driver's IOMMU dependency won't resolve.

CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RKNPU=y is already set in rockchip_linux_defconfig
(this layer's shared kernel config) - no defconfig change needed, this
was purely a devicetree gap.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Yocto Port <elmermetrasbrum@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi
index 4198b86..338048b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi
@@ -821,3 +821,11 @@
 		/* GPIO4_D4-D7 */
 		"", "", "", "";
 };
+
+&rknpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknpu_mmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
